From: a50-halium <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] build.sh: honour SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH for BUILD_DATE

BUILD_DATE is a live `date +%s`, and with GITHUB_REF unset the branch resolves
to "user", which makes SET_LOCALVERSION produce

    LOCALVERSION=" - Mint-user $BUILD_DATE"

so the epoch of the moment the build started is compiled into the kernel
version string. Two builds of identical source therefore never match:

    Linux version 4.14.194 - Mint-user 1788185700 (a50-halium@reproducible)
    Linux version 4.14.194 - Mint-user 1788185793 (a50-halium@reproducible)

Taking SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH when it is set makes the value a property of the pin
rather than of the clock, which is what that variable is for. The fallback is
unchanged, so an ordinary upstream build behaves exactly as before.

diff --git a/build.sh b/build.sh
index 3d48b4417..c7aad831e 100755
--- a/build.sh
+++ b/build.sh
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ VERSION=$(grep -m 1    VERSION "$TOP/Makefile"    | sed 's/^.*= //g')
 PATCHLEVEL=$(grep -m 1 PATCHLEVEL "$TOP/Makefile" | sed 's/^.*= //g')
 SUBLEVEL=$(grep -m 1   SUBLEVEL "$TOP/Makefile"   | sed 's/^.*= //g')
 
-BUILD_DATE="$(date +%s)"
+BUILD_DATE="${SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH:-$(date +%s)}"
 BUILD_KERNEL_BRANCH="${GITHUB_REF##*/}"
 [[ -z $BUILD_KERNEL_BRANCH ]] && BUILD_KERNEL_BRANCH="user"
 [[ $BUILD_KERNEL_BRANCH == *"android-"* ]] && BUILD_KERNEL_BRANCH="mainline"
